# Line endings are LF everywhere, regardless of who checks the repo out.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) and linted, built and
# deployed on Linux. Without this file the working tree gets CRLF, and:
#
#   - prettier's endOfLine default is "lf", so `npx prettier --check .` reports
#     "Delete CR" on all 21,000-odd lines of the tree and buries any real
#     formatting error in the noise. That happened while debugging a CI lint
#     failure and cost a wrong diagnosis before the noise was recognised.
#
# NOTE: this file does NOT fix the other symptom it was originally credited with.
# src/routeTree.gen.ts intermittently shows as modified with an empty diff and
# blocks `git checkout <branch>`. That has a different cause - the repo, .git
# included, sits in a OneDrive Files-On-Demand sync root, and git's default stat
# comparison is unreliable there. See section 8 of
# docs/handoff/2026-09-01-crm-state.md. One symptom, two faults; do not assume
# this file addressed both.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalises to LF in the index (already true here) and
# checks LF back out, so a Windows working tree matches what CI sees. It changes
# no stored content.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated by the build and committed; CI fails if it is stale, so it must
# round-trip byte-for-byte.
src/routeTree.gen.ts text eol=lf

# Leave binaries alone.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
